assets/robot/kr16_2.glb
-----------------------

A visual model of a six-axis industrial arm, used only to draw the welding cell
(dashboard/static/cell3d.js and scripts/build_cell_blender.py). Nothing is
measured or scored against it.

Source
  The kuka_kr16_support package of ROS-Industrial kuka_experimental:
  https://github.com/ros-industrial/kuka_experimental
  The package manifest names Lars Tingelstad as its author.

Licence
  The kuka_experimental repository is distributed under the Apache License,
  Version 2.0. The kuka_kr16_support package manifest (package.xml) declares
  BSD instead. The two statements disagree and it is not settled here which one
  the upstream authors intend for this package. No copyright line was recorded
  when the model was brought into this repository, so this notice does not
  reproduce one, and it does not reproduce BSD licence text either. What it
  gives is the attribution above and the record of changes below. If the BSD
  reading is the one that applies, the copyright line, conditions and disclaimer
  are still owed here, once the holder is confirmed from the upstream package.

Changes from the upstream files
  The kr16_2 robot description and its visual meshes were imported into NVIDIA
  Isaac Sim with its URDF importer, saved as USD, and converted to binary glTF
  with the Omniverse glTF converter. The file's own header records that last
  step ("Exported from Omniverse GLTF Converter."). The converter renamed some
  parts (for example tn__Link3Motor1_lB6) and wrote no copyright field into the
  file, which is why this notice exists.

  The description that was imported is a copy prepared for the Isaac Sim
  importer (kr16_2_isaac.urdf), not the upstream kr16_2 file itself. It has not
  been compared line by line with upstream, so this notice does not claim the
  geometry is unchanged.
